hey there my name is max and i'm joined  today by  jordan hello and today we're going to be  talking about apex legends  season 7. now we got the chance to play  early and we got to see a lot  of the new content coming to apex  legends right now we know there's a  whole bunch of stuff coming such as  clubs  new battle pass new vehicle a new legend  new map  jordan what do you think of the map so  far i really  like olympus from what we've seen so far  we only had a few  hours of hands-on time but it's exciting  for the first  time in a really long time apex legends  feels like it's on the brink of  delivering us  something completely brand new olympus  is  this fat chunky boy of a map it's  bigger than king's canyon but smaller  than  world's edge so world's edge will still  hold the title as the largest map  in apex legends it's not really divided  into halves the same way  that kings canyon and world's edge are  it's more like these  distinct zones these biomes all around  the outside and they all surround this  one  giant location kind of in the middle and  it creates a very  different looking map as well as a very  like different type of  loot chase that you have when you decide  to land on it  for sure i could almost say that it's so  well designed that it's hard to tell  where the new skull town is going to be  yeah there's no one singular place that  everybody's gone to right now i mean  there is  everybody was exploring for the most  part but even like just thinking ahead  like there's a lot of good hot zones in  this map  and i'm not sure what the next skull  town is going to be at this point  because it's so well designed  and there's also just like a lot of fun  like small easter eggs to discover  too like i thought it was really funny  there was just this moment where we  remembered during the presentation  that olympus has on its map like the  restaurant where revenant  killed loba's parents and i had this  realization at the same time that you  happen to be going like  in that direction and i happen to be  playing as revenant and we had a lobo in  the squad and were like  well what happens when the two of them  go  back to the place where years ago  revenant  killed lopez parents like right in front  of her  i'll see you back here after the match i  have something for you  let's finish this there's all these  other like cool things too like there's  a hammond lab there and if you go there  with horizon  she'll talk about how it wasn't always  called  the hammond labs it used to be named  after someone else since this was  her home like years ago before she got  trapped in the black hole and so there's  all these like really fun  cute and funny like easter eggs to just  discover across the map you can really  tell that they've constructed this map  in mind with the fact that they've now  made it that legends comment on where  they are that they interact with each  other based on who's  in the squad and so the map's been kind  of designed around that mechanic it's  just  full of these little cool things to  discover  respawn has been teasing olympus for a  long time and a lot of  lore has been kind of piling up to this  point and now that there's a whole bunch  of characters able to drop onto the map  i'm sure there's just gonna be a ton of  info drops about what the legends  history is and what happened to them but  you don't have to  completely explore it on your own  there is a new legend that we're getting  with season seven  and her abilities kind of help you  explore this new  vertical space and that's horizon and  specifically  her tactical ability for me personally  horizon  is probably one of my favorite new  season characters i mean lobo was  interesting  i think revenant was really fun but  really weak when he first started out  and then rampart was fairly fun as well  but wasn't really my playstyle  horizon is very movement focused and  very cc focused so it meets crowd  control  those two combined really make me want  to use a tactical and ultimate  more than other legends so her tactical  is a gravity lift which  lifts you up and enemy players this  tactical is  amazing it first of all has a 15 second  cooldown but it has a 10 second active  time so it's only five seconds where you  can't actually use it which is pretty  amazing if you think about it it's great  for just  using in a firefight to dodge gunfire uh  it's great for  reaching really really high areas and  she also has her ultimate which is  everybody's been calling at the zarya  alt right this is just like the black  hole that sucks everybody in  from the time that i played horizon i  didn't really get a good grasp of  exactly how  the black hole works i mean it generally  it pulls everybody in towards the middle  of it  but it's been kind of weird on how  strong that pull is  i just want to get some more time in the  game to really flesh out how that  exactly works  of course her passive really ties in  with everything else too because her  passive reduces her landing lag when she  lands from a really tall area which  everybody else has  i remember back in the day in apex  legends season one and two where  everybody would kick the ground to  reduce landing lag  she has that all the time which is great  and it's really useful for  jumping off at high areas to ambush  people also she has better air control  so she can strafe around areas really  quickly  so she's just a really good movement  based character which really feels good  to play  so of course respawn has been touting as  well that this is their first vehicle  in apex legends the trident is coming  it's a three person vehicle and it's  really cool to drive around but it's not  as op as people have been making it out  to be  yeah i say i've been seeing comments of  people complaining that the  trident's going to make this game like  pubg or  call of duty blackout and that you'll be  able to use the trident to just like run  people  over and get easy kills and it's like  nah nah nah it's not gonna work that way  i don't want to say it's weak but it's  not like something that you want to be  ideally driving into the middle of a  fire fight  at this point going into a firefight  with the trident is pretty bad because  the lag time to get on and off the  vehicle is really really slow  and the damage is shared among all the  players if the shots hit the actual  vehicle itself so everybody takes damage  which makes it tanky but also  you gotta heal which sucks we don't  really know as of right now that it  could be very powerful because  we've seen some legend ability pairing  on it such as caustic traps or even  revenant's totem can be  placed on it you know rampart's turret  can be placed on it as well so  pairing it with abilities which we  didn't test too much i  could make it extremely powerful but as  of right now just on its own it's  not as strong as people say its primary  purpose is to just get  your squad from one side of the map to  the other  that's basically it you can augment its  offensive abilities with specific  legends but  ideally you're just kind of using it  like you would a pathfinder zipline or  wraith portal you're just trying to get  your squad from  point a to point b as quickly as  possible so besides that season seven is  bringing in clubs  a new battle pass with a whole bunch of  new gear also it's going to be bringing  apex legends to steam officially so  that'll bring even more cross-play  players it'll bring in  more people together with the clubs and  the battle pass will obviously give you  lots of new goodies for your legends  so that's our look at season seven  there's a new map there's a new legend  there's a new vehicle there's a whole  bunch of other things as well that are  new that are coming and that's not even  including the patch notes which are  gonna be coming out  explaining all the buffs and nerfs and  other things that are coming to apex  legend season seven  if you like content like this stick  around we've got a whole bunch more  coming including  tests with horizon and a legend guide  with horizon on how to use her and more  to come in the time ahead so  thanks for watching bye you are the apex  [Music]  champions  [Music]  you

